id.instance: String (TS "c<n>")
num.game: i32
num.cursor: u32
map.ordered: IndexMap
bag.data: IndexMap<String, serde_json::Value>
error.style: Result<_, EngineError> with TS's message; panic only on invariants (a TS `toThrow` / `not.toThrow` is a panic / no panic)
null.optional: Option + skip_serializing_if
null.nullable: Option, serialised null
case.json: camelCase via serde rename_all
case.rust: snake_case
state.mut: &mut GameState writes, &GameState reads, &mut EngineSink for TS sink mutators (tests edit their own clones of scenario states)
rng.source: Rng::new(&state.seed, state.rng_cursor) and write the cursor back (tests: create_rng(seed, 0) for TS's createRng(seed))
hook.style: Arc<dyn Fn + Send + Sync> via hook(); no fn pointers, no Box (test fixtures build hooks with hook(); MatchHooks are Box<dyn FnMut + 'a>)
registry.style: OnceLock set once by register_all; fused scripts built on lookup from state (tests: testkit's thread-local override per test)
async.style: tokio in crates/server only; none in pure crates
log.style: tracing JSON to stdout, server only
ai.counter: NodeCounter is a trait (used, limit, take, stopped_by); every search fn takes &mut dyn NodeCounter (tests pass &mut counter)
ai.simstep: simulate -> Option<Result<GameState, String>>
ai.defaults: TS default parameters are explicit arguments; TS optional parameters are Option
test.literals: TS object literals as json!(…) + json_as; answers of types SURFACE does not name compared as JSON
test.cache: TS module-level computed fixtures are OnceLock statics local to the test binary
